(
    // branding card — the brand mark only (zero `Ink`). The mark is
    // aspect-fit inside the body: it scales to the SMALLER of the horizontal
    // slot (a ~0.62 em advance estimate, so a multi-char word shrinks to fit
    // the width first) or the full body height, keeps its aspect, and sits
    // centered with a generous 16 px pad. That fit is computed per frame in
    // `scene_values` (the glyph is re-read from `$states2/d` on every draw, so
    // editing the id shows up with no restart), which is why the mark's size
    // and top ride the new `font_size` / `y` bindings instead of constants.
    //
    // Geometry of record (draw_branding_card): `avail_w = w − 2·16`,
    // `avail_h = h − 24 − 16`, `size = min(avail_w / (chars·0.62), avail_h) ·
    // 0.95` (≥ 10), and the top at `24 + (avail_h − size) / 2` — the same
    // `ui::text_cw` centering the drawer used, with the Brand font.
    items: [
        Header(title: "Brand", glyph: "\u{f004}", pad: 16.0),
        Text(
            x: 0.0,
            center_x: true,
            y: "brand_y",
            w: 0.0,
            text: "{brand_glyph}",
            font_size: "brand_size",
            font: brand,
            color: fg,
            visible: "brand_live",
        ),
        Text(
            // the drawer's own empty caption (`card_empty`), centered
            x: 0.0,
            center_x: true,
            center_y: true,
            y: -6.0,
            w: 0.0,
            text: "no brand glyph in $states2/d",
            font_size: 9.0,
            color: fg3,
            visible: "brand_empty",
        ),
    ],
)
